---
description: NestJS modules, REST contracts, validation, Swagger and tests
globs: "src/**/*.ts,test/**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Follow feature modules and constructor dependency injection. Controllers handle HTTP; services implement business behavior.
- Use validated class DTOs compatible with the global whitelist/forbidNonWhitelisted/transform ValidationPipe. Preserve runtime DTO imports for decorators.
- Keep response DTOs and Swagger metadata accurate, including the named `JWT-auth` bearer scheme. Swagger lives at `/api/docs`; this is not a global route prefix.
- Preserve API contracts unless the requested change requires an update. Use Nest exceptions for expected failures.
- Use injected PrismaService and explicit safe response fields.
- Verify TypeScript changes with lint, build and relevant Jest tests. HTTP tests should reproduce production pipes and guards; unit tests should mock database dependencies.
